From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hayaksi1 <193020925+hayaksi1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 20:40:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Carry the spoiler snapshot over to the vitest format

This suite never executed until the environment pragma landed, so its
snapshot file still held a jest-era key that nothing had rewritten. Now
that the test runs, vitest records the same value under its own key format
and the old entry is left orphaned. The recorded markup is unchanged, so
this only settles which key the value lives under.
---
 .../web/src/slash-commands/__snapshots__/spoiler.test.ts.snap | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/apps/web/src/slash-commands/__snapshots__/spoiler.test.ts.snap b/apps/web/src/slash-commands/__snapshots__/spoiler.test.ts.snap
index 06e6a7dfc5..6099d666d7 100644
--- a/apps/web/src/slash-commands/__snapshots__/spoiler.test.ts.snap
+++ b/apps/web/src/slash-commands/__snapshots__/spoiler.test.ts.snap
@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
-// Jest Snapshot v1, https://jestjs.io/docs/snapshot-testing
+// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html
 
-exports[`/spoiler should wrap the message in a spoiler span 1`] = `"<span data-mx-spoiler>this is a test message</span>"`;
+exports[`/spoiler > should wrap the message in a spoiler span 1`] = `"<span data-mx-spoiler>this is a test message</span>"`;
